spans.s:
पौरव f. ई descended from or belonging to Pūru;
 m. a
descendant of P., pl. his race, N. of a people.

पौराण f. ई belonging to or derived from the olden
times;
 primeval, ancient.

पौरुष॑ f. ई human, manly, belonging or consecrated to
Puruṣa. —m. a man's load;
 f. ई a woman;
 n. manhood, virility, manly
deed, a man's length.

पौ॑रुषेय f. ई a relating to man, human. —m.
hireling, day-labourer;
 n. human deed or work.

पौर्णमास॑ f. ई॑ relating to the full moon;
 m. n.
festival of the full moon;
 n. day of full moon;
 f. ई day or night of
full moon.

पौर्वापर्य n. priority and posteriority;
 succession,
continuity.
